@@ doc_halts_budget
On every input on which the $build build is never refused memory for exceeding $budget, and when the environment refuses nothing it is not forced to, every execution of the $build build exits with $exits.  It never crashes, fails an assertion, hangs, or leaves the model.$rejected$binds$note

Not claimed: anything about what the program writes; anything about other compilers, architectures or $library_name commits.

@@ doc_halts_may_fail
Every execution of the $build build exits, with $exits, on every input and whatever the environment refuses (any allocation, open or read may fail at any time).$rejected$stronger$binds$note$no_asan

Not claimed: anything about what the program writes.

@@ no_asan
  There is no ASan statement of this form: the ASan runtime deliberately waits forever when its start-up reservation is refused, so such a statement would be false for a reason that has nothing to do with this $who.

@@ stronger
  It covers every input and any refusal, unlike [$budget_name], but allows any exit status.

@@ rejected
  Status 78 is the driver's report that a call of the fuzz target returned a value other than 0 or -1, which this fuzz target does to turn an input away ($where).

@@ binds_one
  Check $letters ends the process when it fails, which this statement excludes, so a proof establishes it for the code in this binary on every input it covers.
@@ binds_many
  Checks $letters each end the process when they fail, which this statement excludes, so a proof establishes them for the code in this binary on every input it covers.

@@ note_plain

@@ note_ubsan
  A failed UBSan check traps, so a proof also shows that no check UBSan makes in this build fails on any such input.
@@ note_ubsan_rust
  A failed rustc UB check writes its source location on standard error and exits with status 79, which is not allowed, and a failed UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer check in C code traps, so a proof also shows that no UB check this build makes fails on any such input.
@@ note_ubsan_rust_any
  A failed UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer check in C code traps, so a proof also shows that none fails on any such input.  A failed rustc UB check exits with status 79, which this statement allows: it says nothing about those checks.
@@ stronger_rust
  It covers every input and any refusal, unlike [$budget_name], but allows any exit status: a panic, which exits with status 79, does not falsify it.
@@ note_asan
  An ASan report aborts, so a proof also shows that ASan detects no memory error, in the code it instruments, on any such input (the harness README lists the code this build links uninstrumented).  The runtime's own address-space reservations are not charged to the budget.
@@ note_asan-ubsan
  An ASan report aborts and a failed UBSan check traps, so a proof also shows that neither sanitizer fires, in the code they instrument, on any such input (the harness README lists the code this build links uninstrumented).
@@ note_asan-ubsan_rust
  An ASan report aborts, a failed rustc UB check exits with status 79, which is not allowed, and a failed UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer check in C code traps, so a proof also shows that none of them fires, in the code they instrument, on any such input (the harness README lists the code this build links uninstrumented).

@@ doc_agreement
On every input on which the plain build is never refused memory for exceeding $plain_budget, $environment: neither build ever faults, aborts or leaves the model, and the two write the same bytes and exit with the same status.  $san_note$variant

Not claimed: anything about inputs on which the plain build needs more than $plain_budget$not_claimed.

@@ env_may-fail
whatever the environment refuses in either build
@@ env_alloc-forced-only
when a memory request is refused only if the budget is spent or no address range is free (any other request may still be refused, in either build)

@@ agree_ubsan
A failed UBSan check traps, so a proof shows that no UBSan check in this build fails on any such input.
@@ agree_ubsan_rust
A failed rustc UB check writes its source location on standard error and exits with status 79, a line the plain build, which makes no such check, does not write at that point, and a failed UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer check in C code traps, so a proof shows that no UB check this build makes fails on any such input.
@@ agree_asan
An ASan report aborts, so a proof shows that ASan reports nothing on any such input: no memory error that this build's ASan detects happens in the code it instruments (the harness, $library_name and the driver, less the code the harness README lists as uninstrumented).
@@ agree_asan-ubsan
An ASan report aborts and a failed UBSan check traps, so a proof shows that neither sanitizer fires on any such input in the code they instrument (the harness, $library_name and the driver, less the code the harness README lists as uninstrumented).
@@ agree_asan_python
An ASan report aborts, so a proof shows that ASan reports nothing on any such input: no memory error that this build's ASan detects happens in the code it instruments (the C code: the CPython interpreter, which runs the harness and $library_name as bytecode, the port's interpreter host, and the driver, less the code the harness README lists as uninstrumented).
@@ agree_asan-ubsan_python
An ASan report aborts and a failed UBSan check traps, so a proof shows that neither sanitizer fires on any such input in the code they instrument (the C code: the CPython interpreter, which runs the harness and $library_name as bytecode, the port's interpreter host, and the driver, less the code the harness README lists as uninstrumented).
@@ agree_asan-ubsan_rust
An ASan report aborts and a failed UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer check in C code traps; a failed rustc UB check writes its source location on standard error and exits with status 79, a line the plain build, which makes no such check, does not write at that point.  So a proof shows that none of them fires on any such input in the code they instrument (the harness, $library_name and the driver, less the code the harness README lists as uninstrumented).

@@ not_claimed_asan
; memory errors ASan does not detect (for example an access that lands inside another live object, or one made in code it does not instrument)

@@ variant_abort
  Stated with abort() read as death by SIGABRT rather than as a step the model does not cover; the statement still forbids it.
@@ variant_rv64gc
  The process is told that its machine is RV64GC (no vector unit).
@@ variant_alloc_rust
  It is read alloc-forced-only because the allocation-failure hook writes the failed allocation's size on standard error, and ASan's allocator asks the kernel for memory at other allocations than musl's: refused at will, the two builds could write different lines for a reason that has nothing to do with ASan.
@@ variant_own_budgets
  This statement has this project's own budgets: $plain for the plain build (default $plain_default) and $san for the $san_build build (default $san_default).  The project's notes say why.
@@ variant_alloc_python
  It is read alloc-forced-only because CPython ends with abort() (a fatal error) when some allocations it makes while it starts are refused: refused at will, both builds could abort for a reason that has nothing to do with the sanitizer.

@@ doc_bound
For an input drawn from [Distribution.w] (Distribution.v), the probability that the plain and $san builds are not both error-free with equal traces is at most [b].  Agreement here is judged at 16 GiB / 512 GiB with no budget premise (Core.Shapes), so [$agrees] does not by itself give [$name 0].  Smaller [b] is stronger; [b = 1] holds trivially.

@@ doc_decidability
Some well-formed riscv64 program decides exactly the finite inputs on which the plain and $san builds agree ([Characterise.v] states the problem for a given program).

@@ proving
A proof is a directory proofs/$project/$harness/<statement>/ whose Proof.v ends, for example, in
  Theorem ${example}_holds : Statements.$example.
$bound_example
See docs/proving.md.

@@ bound_example
A bound proof names its bound:
  Theorem ${name}_holds : Statements.$name (1 # 1000).

